 "subs": [
  {
   "text": "322 files",
   "start": 17.026,
   "duration": 15.351,
   "x": -560,
   "y": -230,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "3.71 GB",
   "start": 17.476,
   "duration": 14.901,
   "x": 560,
   "y": -230,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "794 reviews",
   "start": 17.926,
   "duration": 14.451,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "2h 36m median",
   "start": 18.376,
   "duration": 14.001,
   "x": 560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Two of the most upvoted reviews on this Steam demo say\nthe same thing. It's a crypto miner. Don't install it.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "duration": 6.681
  },
  {
   "text": "It isn't. But I know why they think that,\nand it's sitting in the game's own file list.",
   "start": 6.931,
   "duration": 5.845
  },
  {
   "text": "This is Nomad Drive. You repair a rundown RV and drive it across a\nprocedurally generated wasteland, alone or with up to three friends.",
   "start": 16.626,
   "duration": 9.188
  },
  {
   "text": "The demo went up on June fifteenth. Right now, while I'm\nrecording this, about two thousand people are inside it.",
   "start": 26.064,
   "duration": 6.263
  },
  {
   "text": "Seven hundred ninety four recent reviews, seventy one\npercent positive. Steam calls that Mostly Positive.",
   "start": 32.577,
   "duration": 7.412
  },
  {
   "text": "The number that made me pick this one: the median reviewer had\ntwo hours and thirty six minutes on it before they wrote anything.",
   "start": 40.239,
   "duration": 7.412
  },
  {
   "text": "Two and a half hours, in a free demo. Nobody is bouncing off\nthis. Some of them just think it's mining crypto while they play.",
   "start": 47.901,
   "duration": 8.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Those two things have the same cause, and I can show\nyou, because Steam publishes a file list for every demo.",
   "start": 56.451,
   "duration": 6.994
  },
  {
   "text": "Three hundred and twenty two entries. Three point seven gigabytes.\nNo unpacking, no decompiling, nothing private. Just names and sizes.",
   "start": 63.695,
   "duration": 8.352
  },
  {
   "text": "Start with the engine. The\nfirst line is already odd.",
   "start": 72.297,
   "duration": 4.121
  },
  {
   "text": "It's Unity. But it's the High Definition Render Pipeline, and there's\na GPU driven runtime in there too, which puts it on Unity six.",
   "start": 76.668,
   "duration": 9.136
  },
  {
   "text": "Almost every small team picks the Universal pipeline instead. It's\nlighter and it runs on anything. HDRP looks better and costs more to run.",
   "start": 86.054,
   "duration": 10.338
  },
  {
   "text": "Which brings us back to the crypto miner. There is no miner in that file list. What\nthere is, is a very expensive renderer and, apparently, nothing capping the frame rate.",
   "start": 96.642,
   "duration": 9.685
  },
  {
   "text": "Players reported ninety nine percent GPU load sitting in\nthe menu. On a five thousand series card. Doing nothing.",
   "start": 106.577,
   "duration": 7.281
  },
  {
   "text": "That's what an uncapped render loop looks like from outside. Your fans\nspin up on a menu screen, and you assume something is stealing from you.",
   "start": 114.108,
   "duration": 8.614
  },
  {
   "text": "So that's the look. What about the driving,\nwhich is the entire point of the game?",
   "start": 122.972,
   "duration": 4.904
  },
  {
   "text": "They licensed it. Vehicle Physics two, its wheel\ncontroller, and the multiplayer add on that ships with it.",
   "start": 128.126,
   "duration": 6.054
  },
  {
   "text": "Which is the right call. Writing a vehicle simulator is a\nyear of your life, easily. Nobody should be doing that twice.",
   "start": 134.43,
   "duration": 7.961
  },
  {
   "text": "Same story for the world. The terrain is MapMagic\ntwo, a node graph that generates the map at runtime.",
   "start": 142.641,
   "duration": 6.21
  },
  {
   "text": "That explains a complaint that shows up over and over in\nthe Chinese reviews. It gets repetitive a few hours in.",
   "start": 149.101,
   "duration": 9.215
  },
  {
   "text": "And there are only four scenes in the whole build, the biggest one half\na megabyte. The gigabytes are all loot and locations, streamed in.",
   "start": 158.566,
   "duration": 7.961
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the co-op, which is where\na small team usually drowns.",
   "start": 166.777,
   "duration": 3.781
  },
  {
   "text": "Mirror, which is free and open source, running over the Epic Online\nServices relay, with Steam lobbies next to it and Vivox for voice.",
   "start": 170.808,
   "duration": 8.535
  },
  {
   "text": "Server bill, zero. That shows up in the reviews too. Two players in the same\ncity, five kilometres apart, getting three to four hundred milliseconds.",
   "start": 179.593,
   "duration": 9.554
  },
  {
   "text": "That's not a bug in their code. That's what a free global\nrelay does. Your traffic goes wherever the relay happens to be.",
   "start": 189.397,
   "duration": 6.759
  },
  {
   "text": "So the driving is bought, the world is bought, the\nnetcode is bought. What did they actually build?",
   "start": 196.406,
   "duration": 6.263
  },
  {
   "text": "Sixteen assemblies of their own. Dependency injection, save system,\nlocalization, input, audio, settings, and the glue over Mirror.",
   "start": 202.919,
   "duration": 7.778
  },
  {
   "text": "That is a studio framework. Whoever is behind\nIndie Devil has shipped software before.",
   "start": 210.947,
   "duration": 5.218
  },
  {
   "text": "Although they also shipped a folder that Unity itself names Do\nNot Ship, and left every asset package's sample code in the build.",
   "start": 216.415,
   "duration": 7.83
  },
  {
   "text": "That's what shipping fast looks like. In the reviews, driving is what people\ntalk about most, and performance is what they complain about loudest.",
   "start": 224.495,
   "duration": 8.352
  },
  {
   "text": "And the split is telling. Positive reviewers had played three hours\nand eighteen minutes. Negative reviewers, one hour and twelve.",
   "start": 233.097,
   "duration": 7.935
  },
  {
   "text": "The word potential shows up in fifty positive reviews and two negative\nones. People aren't asking for a finished game. They want it to run.",
   "start": 241.282,
   "duration": 8.901
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the whole\nteardown on one card.",
   "start": 250.433,
   "duration": 2.266
  },
  {
   "text": "Unity six on HDRP. Team size never disclosed. Public devlogs going back to twenty\ntwenty four. Mirror, Epic Online Services, MapMagic, and Vehicle Physics two.",
   "start": 252.949,
   "duration": 11.879
  },
  {
   "text": "And the trick, if you want one: they licensed every hard\nsystem and spent their own time on the glue and the content.",
   "start": 265.078,
   "duration": 7.517
  },
  {
   "text": "Worth a dip. Early access is set for September\nthirtieth, and the demo is free right now.",
   "start": 272.845,
   "duration": 5.505
  },
  {
   "text": "If you're shipping a demo this year, the lesson costs you one afternoon.\nCap your frame rate in the menu, or the internet will decide you're a miner.",
   "start": 278.6,
   "duration": 7.961
  },
  {
   "text": "Next time, another demo, another\nfile list. This is Demo Dip.",
   "start": 286.811,
   "duration": 4.434
  }
 ],
